## What the finding objects to
The only assertion names a feeling ("Ada feels welcomed by what the greeter prints"), so a reviewer must judge what counts as welcoming. The user settled what counts as correct: the greeter prints exactly the configured greeting, then the name, on one line — asserted as the stdout pattern `^Hello Ada$`, as a single Then step — and the description states that behaviour instead of the feeling.

The behaviour stays the same: the same Given (greeting configured as "Hello") and the same When (the Operator runs "greet Ada") lead to the same printed line; only the words of the outcome change, from a feeling to the observable output. The rewritten Then step fills the existing catalogue template `stdout matches {expected:pattern}` (block `then`), whose `{expected:pattern}` slot is the rest of the step verbatim.

